## Phase 1 — Storage and data layer (SQL)
- Use SQLAlchemy with SQLite by default, written so Postgres can be swapped in via config.
- Proposed tables: `instruments` (ticker, asset class, metadata, data basis),
  `timeseries` (long format: ticker, field, date, value, source, fetched_at),
  `events` (type, datetime, actual, consensus, prior), `positions`,
  `fundamentals` (manual and Bloomberg inputs with source and publication date),
  `fetch_log`.
- Incremental updates only fetch missing dates. Bloomberg has data limits: batch
  requests, never refetch cached data, log request counts per run.
- Store PUBLICATION date as well as reference date for every fundamental and positioning
  series, so analytics can avoid lookahead. Examples: CFTC data is as of Tuesday but
  released Friday; inventory and trade data publish with lags.
- Trading session alignment: LME, COMEX and SHFE close at different times. Document
  the alignment choice and make it configurable.
- Include a ticker verification report: every configured ticker and field is tested,
  and failures or sparse series are listed, never silently skipped.

