## Phase 6 — Volatility
1. Surface monitor: ATM term structure, risk reversals and butterflies for gold and
   copper; percentile vs history.
2. Variance risk premium: implied vol minus subsequently realised vol, by metal,
   tenor and regime. Use correctly lagged realised windows.
3. Event vol: implied move priced before FOMC and CPI vs realised move afterwards,
   for gold and copper.
4. Cross-asset vol RV: gold vol vs USDJPY and EURUSD vol; copper vol vs AUDUSD and
   USDCNH vol; metals vol vs MOVE. Rolling correlations, ratio z-scores, and a
   regression-implied fair value with residuals.
5. Skew signals: does gold call skew or copper put skew lead spot moves or
   realised vol changes?
6. Note data quality issues explicitly: historical options data for metals can be
   patchy. Report gaps and do not interpolate silently.

## Phase 7 — Risk module
- Positions table in SQL (futures and options; strike, expiry, type, quantity).
- Price futures options with Black-76. Compute delta, gamma, vega, theta per position
  and aggregated.
- Daily P&L attribution: delta, gamma, vega, theta, and unexplained residual. Large
  unexplained P&L must be flagged.
- Stress grid: spot ±2/5/10% × vol ±2/5/10 points, plus named scenarios
  (e.g. "dollar +3%, real yields +25bp", "China stimulus: copper +8%, vol −3").
- Include a synthetic example book so the module can be demonstrated end to end.

